WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.740
Without Notch, a fly embryo builds too much nervous system and too little skin.

2
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.140
Notch is what lets a cell be told, not you.

3
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.900
But the message never leaves the cell that makes it.

4
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.980
The ligand is a protein fixed in that cell's membrane, and the receptor is fixed in

5
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.820
its neighbour's. The two can meet only where cells touch.

6
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:30.653
Binding is not enough.

7
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:37.393
Just outside the membrane, Notch is folded into a lock that hides the spot where it

8
00:00:37.393 --> 00:00:42.113
can be cut. In the standard account, the receptor must be pulled.

9
00:00:42.953 --> 00:00:48.593
The sending cell draws its ligand back inside, and the tug passes to the receptor it

10
00:00:48.593 --> 00:00:52.093
holds. The pull peels the lock open.

11
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:58.533
In mammalian cells, the first cut comes while the receptor is made, and it carries

12
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:05.093
no signal. After the pull, an ADAM protease makes the second cut, just outside the

13
00:01:05.093 --> 00:01:10.353
membrane. The outer part leaves with the ligand, and a stub stays in the membrane.

14
00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:15.173
Then γ-secretase makes the third cut, inside the membrane.

15
00:01:15.173 --> 00:01:21.293
It accepts a membrane protein only after most of the outer part is gone, so the

16
00:01:21.293 --> 00:01:22.453
second cut comes first.

17
00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:28.347
That cut frees the inner part of the receptor, which is called NICD.

18
00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:34.187
It enters the nucleus, where a protein called CSL already sits on the target genes.

19
00:01:34.887 --> 00:01:39.527
In the standard account, CSL keeps those genes off with co-repressors.

20
00:01:40.287 --> 00:01:46.087
NICD binds CSL, displaces the co-repressors, and recruits a co-activator called

21
00:01:46.087 --> 00:01:48.287
Mastermind. The genes turn on.

22
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:55.600
In a kinase cascade, each active enzyme modifies many substrates, so the signal

23
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.260
grows at every step.

24
00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.240
Notch has no second messenger and no kinase relay.

25
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.720
Between the membrane and the gene, nothing multiplies.

26
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.140
One cut receptor gives one inner part.

27
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.120
A cut cannot be undone, so each receptor signals once.

28
00:02:15.983 --> 00:02:19.683
What this design buys the cell is a count.

29
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:26.443
The amount of inner part follows, one for one, the number of receptors a neighbour

30
00:02:26.443 --> 00:02:27.843
has pulled and cut.

31
00:02:28.743 --> 00:02:32.083
A cell hears Notch only from the cells it touches.

32
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:39.743
Keep this rule: one receptor, pulled and cut, gives one inner part and one message.
